{"ts": "2026-07-29T00:23:31", "session": "20260729-002242", "seq": 1, "kind": "note", "note": "verdict(stream): No alignment produced green, so the tail is not RGB triplets.\n\n  start 9: red - whole diamond, but slighlty darker than full brightness\n  start 10: red - the same as before\n  start 11: red - the same as before\n\n  intensity test: red - but brighter\n\nThe bytes still control which LEDs light \u2014 bisection established\nthat. So they are most likely per-LED intensity with the colour\nfixed by something else, or a packed format wider than one byte per\nchannel. Colour control is not solved and may need a different\nopcode entirely."}
